# Devoted Duelist: haste lets it attack the turn it is cast (Bot1 T1), and flurry pings each opponent on Bot1's second spell
# of a turn only: not its first, not its third, and not Bot2's own second spell (T2), which also leaves Ajani, an opponent's
# planeswalker, untouched since the damage goes to each opponent and not to what they control. The Duelist cast as Bot1's
# second spell on T1 does not trigger itself.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Devoted Duelist
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Ajani Resolute
Plains x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Devoted Duelist.Cast
[T1 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Attack(Devoted Duelist > Bot2)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ajani Resolute.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield.Ajani Resolute.Counters.Loyalty = 2
